.SH "NAME"
warp\-workers\-create\-employee \- Create Employee
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B warp workers create\-employee
\fB\-\-first\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-last\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-position\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-start\-date\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-email\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-department\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-manager\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-work\-location\fR \fI<value>\fR \fB\-\-compensation\fR \fI<json>\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Create a new US employee. The worker will be created in draft status and must be invited separately via the invite endpoint. If hiring in a state without an existing tax registration, you must specify the stateRegistration field.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-first\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
a non empty string. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-last\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
a non empty string. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-position\fR \fI<value>\fR
The employee's job title. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-date\fR \fI<value>\fR
A date string in the form YYYY\-MM\-DD. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<value>\fR
Personal email address. The invite will be sent here. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-work\-email\fR \fI<value>\fR
Company\-issued email address, if applicable.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-i9\fR
Whether the employee is required to complete I\-9 work authorization. Set to false if the employee has already been verified off\-platform. Defaults to true.
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-registration\fR \fI<value>\fR
How state tax registration is handled for this employee's work state. Required when hiring in a state where your company doesn't have an existing registration. Use 'self_managed' if you've already registered in this state, or 'warp_managed' for Warp to handle registration on your behalf.
.TP
\fB\-\-department\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
The department to assign this employee to. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-manager\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
The worker id of this employee's direct manager. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-stock\-options\fR \fI<number>\fR
Number of stock options granted to this employee.
.TP
\fB\-\-work\-location\fR \fI<value>\fR
Where the employee will work. Either an existing company workplace or a remote US state. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-compensation\fR \fI<json>\fR
The employee's base compensation. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-compensation.amount\fR \fI<number>\fR
a positive number.
.TP
\fB\-\-compensation.per\fR \fI<value>\fR
Whether the amount is per hour or per year.
.TP
\fB\-\-pay\-schedule\fR \fI<value>\fR
The employee's pay schedule. Must be a pay schedule that the company has configured.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
Override the base URL for API requests.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
